From: ChatGPT <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mtk: mt_wifi: include SAE definitions for DOT11_SAE_SUPPORT

sec_cmm.h embeds pwd_id_list, sae_capability and sae_pk_cfg when either
DOT11_SAE_SUPPORT or SUPP_SAE_SUPPORT is enabled. However, it only
includes sae_cmm.h when SUPP_SAE_SUPPORT is defined.

When DOT11_SAE_SUPPORT is enabled without SUPP_SAE_SUPPORT, those
members have incomplete types and mt_wifi fails to compile. Use the same
condition for including sae_cmm.h as for the embedded SAE fields.

---
 a/mt_wifi/embedded/include/security/sec_cmm.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mt_wifi/embedded/include/security/sec_cmm.h b/mt_wifi/embedded/include/security/sec_cmm.h
--- a/mt_wifi/embedded/include/security/sec_cmm.h
+++ b/mt_wifi/embedded/include/security/sec_cmm.h
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@
 
 
 #include "security/owe_cmm.h"
 
-#ifdef SUPP_SAE_SUPPORT
+#if defined(DOT11_SAE_SUPPORT) || defined(SUPP_SAE_SUPPORT)
 #include "security/sae_cmm.h"
 #endif
 
